:name: U400 BLE bring-up experiment (Stage 1 feasibility probe)
:description: Boots the Aqara U400 Aliro firmware on the emulated EFR32MG24 (brd4186c) and attempts to push it PAST the radio-PA-config spin (0x808105c) toward BLE advertising. Applies the validated least-invasive firmware-side knobs (force the RAIL radio-config primitives to succeed) and samples PC over time to MAP the cascade of radio-init walls. FINDING: the walls are a cascade of RAIL radio-config asserts that all bottom out in ONE unmodeled dependency -- the EFR32 radio config-object / RF-calibration machinery. Each firmware-side bypass only reveals the next assert. Stock firmware advertises in this same rig (BLE transport is intact -- see e2e-15.4.resc).

$bin=@/home/chen/aliro-renode/matter/aliro-u400/firmware/U400_primary_target.elf
$vtor=0x08006000
include @scripts/silabs-vuln/boot_mg24.resc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Least-invasive firmware-side knobs. Each forces a RAIL radio-config primitive
# to return 0 (success): "movs r0,#0 ; bx lr" = WriteWord 0x2000 then 0x4770.
# These primitives (sub_80e3xxx family) all FAIL against the emulated radio
# because the config-object computation reads radio state/calibration the model
# returns as 0. Patching them one-by-one just marches to the next assert:
#
#   (no patch)                     -> 0x808105c  (wall #1: PA-config sub_80e3d60)
#   +0x80e3d60                     -> 0x80fd44e  (wall #3a: sub_80e3e56 assert)
#   +0x80e3e56                     -> 0x80fd45a  (wall #3b: sub_80e3e86 assert)
#   +the 0x80fd4xx cluster (below) -> 0x803e736  (wall #4: sub_80e3dce assert x3)
#
# NOTE: do NOT NOP the eventual RAC/SYNTH and I2C poll loops (sub_803266c etc.);
# NOPing poll-loop back-edges corrupts control flow and core-dumps. Those loops
# spin because the modeled radio never reaches "operational/locked" and the lock's
# I2C peripherals (motor/SE/sensors) have no bus slaves -- both need a real model.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# wall #1: PA-config
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3d60 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3d62 0x4770
# wall #3 cluster primitives (wrapped by asserts at 0x80fd440/44e/45a/468)
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e46 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e48 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e56 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e58 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e86 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e88 0x4770
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e96 0x2000
sysbus WriteWord 0x80e3e98 0x4770

echo ">>> Booting U400 with RAIL radio-config bypass; sampling PC (expect stall at 0x803e736 -- next radio-config assert):"
emulation RunFor "0.2"
echo "PC @0.2s:"; sysbus.cpu PC
emulation RunFor "0.8"
echo "PC @1.0s:"; sysbus.cpu PC
emulation RunFor "2.0"
echo "PC @3.0s:"; sysbus.cpu PC
pause
quit
